    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a `timezone` field to the owner response, derived from the locality/region via the fixed IANA table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nChanges, kept to small cohesive units to minimize structural impact:\n\n1. **`mapper/Timezone.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny pure helper mirroring the existing `Locality`/`ContactPreference` pattern: a single static `of(region)` that looks up the region-to-timezone table, returning `null` for regions not in it.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one new `@Mapping` line. It reuses the exact region derivation already used for `locality` (customer-code prefix, else `Locality.of(postcode, city)`) and feeds it to `Timezone.of(...)`, so timezone always agrees with the reported locality.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the read-only `timezone` string field on the owner schema (the DTO is code-generated from this).\n\nThe unknown-region case yields `null`, so the field is simply absent then \u2014 consistent with how `ageBand` behaves.",
